    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "You can now take a flat dollar amount off an invoice as a discount, as well as a percentage. The acceptance test passes under `bin/e2e`: a $200 subtotal with a $30 flat discount shows $30.00 off and a $170.00 total.\n\nI also called the discount endpoint directly. On a $300 invoice with 10% tax, $30 off gives a $270 taxable amount, $27 tax and a $297 total. Switching back to a 10% discount works, and a negative amount is rejected. I didn't try the new form controls in a browser; the test only checks seeded data.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V41__invoice_discount_amount.sql`, adds a `discount_amount` column. It defaults to 0 and can't be negative, so existing invoices don't change.\n- **Server:** if an invoice has both, the percentage comes off first and then the flat amount. The flat amount is spread across the lines by size so tax and levy are still worked out line by line. It's capped so the discount can never be more than the subtotal. The discount endpoint takes an optional `discountAmount` next to `discountPct`, so existing callers still work. The invoice details now include `discountAmount`, and the test seed endpoint accepts it too.\n- **Front end:** the Discount form has a choice between \"A percentage\" and \"A fixed amount\", with the matching input for each. Applying one clears the other. The discount row reads \"Discount ($30.00 off)\" for a flat amount and \"Discount (X%)\" otherwise.\n\n**New `data-testid`s:** `invoice-discount-amount`, `discount-form-type-pct`, `discount-form-type-amount`, `discount-form-amount` and `discount-form-amount-error`. No existing ones were renamed or removed.\n\n**Two things to know**\n- The server accepts a percentage and a flat amount together, but the form only lets you set one at a time.\n- `invoice-discount-pct` is only on the page when a percentage is shown. When there's just a flat discount, the label shows the amount instead.",
